This is a basic project that shows how to contanerize a flask application.

Dockerfile - Here a multistage docker build was used to reduce image.

**NOTE:**
Flask and similar progreams usually binds to 127.0.0.1. When using docker it is safe practice to add host='0.0.0.0'
 app.run(debug=True, host='0.0.0.0')

 Requirements.txt - Points to necessary extensions to run our application.

It is provisioned with a Github actions workflow which triggers on push and pull

The resource used is AWS, the terraform files configure running apps on aws, stores to s3 bucket and exposes the alb link for accessibility 

